cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "V2VA: Volume Token Volume Alignment across Embedding and Volumetric Spaces for 3D Medical Image Classification"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hao
    given-names: Herbert
    affiliation: "Xiamen University, School of Aerospace Engineering"
    email: "3080942941@qq.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Herbert23H/V2VA-Volume-Token-Volume-Alignment"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
abstract: >-
  V2VA aligns the embedding space of a 3D ViT encoder with the volumetric space of
  the input. JEPA-style self-supervised pretraining learns the volume-to-token
  direction; the classification head applies the reverse token-to-volume direction
  by re-folding encoder tokens [B, N, E] into a voxel grid classified by a residual
  3D CNN. Accepted at PRICAI 2026; the official proceedings are not published yet.
keywords:
  - self-supervised learning
  - medical imaging
  - 3D vision transformer
  - V-JEPA
  - MedMNIST
